home_rules_title = Five rules
home_rules_note = A floor must satisfy every rule that applies. The generator redraws from a derived seed, up to a fixed number of attempts, and reports any violation that remains.
home_rule_1 = Connectivity
home_rule_1_text = Every room can be reached from every other.
home_rule_2 = Clearances
home_rule_2_text = Rooms keep their distance, and corridors keep clear of the rooms they do not join.
home_rule_3 = Doors
home_rule_3_text = Each door fits its room, and doors of one room do not crowd each other.
home_rule_4 = Corridors
home_rule_4_text = Directions, bends and lengths stay within the limits.
home_rule_5 = Entrance and exit
home_rule_5_text = When asked for, there is an entrance and a distinct exit far enough away.
home_rules_link = The rules, in the model
home_same_title = Same seed, same floor
home_same_text = The seed and the parameters fully decide the floor, in the desktop app, in the browser and in the crate. A hash of every stage is compared between builds, and CI checks the WebAssembly build against the native one.
home_params_title = One definition of every parameter
home_params_text = Each parameter is defined once, in the schema crate, with its label and help text. The desktop app, the lab and the parameter reference are generated from it. Parameters copy as JSON.
